# proactive-environmental-sensor-precondition-surfacing

Multiple distinct environmental conditions independently degrade DryWave 3000 sensor accuracy or unit performance: coil icing or overheating (monitored by thermal feedback sensors), rapid humidity dilution from door openings, and steam condensation on the air intake surface. These preconditions must be surfaced proactively whenever advising on operation, interpreting humidity readings, or recommending long-term unattended use — not solely when the user explicitly queries about sensor reliability.

## Procedures
- When advising on long-term unattended operation, proactively note the role of thermal feedback sensors in preventing coil icing or overheating.
- When interpreting or advising on humidity readings, note that door openings can cause rapid sensor reading drops.
- Warn that steam condensation on the air intake can accumulate liquid and reduce long-term performance.
- Do not wait for the user to ask about sensor reliability — surface relevant environmental preconditions in context.

